{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>וככה</b> Two times in the Masorah: וככה תאכלו אותו, and וככה יהיה נעור by Ezra, when he adjured the members of the exile to abandon the burdens. For the second coming is linked to the first coming, as they expounded: it would have been fitting for a miracle to be done for them in the days of Ezra as was done in the days of Moses, except that sin caused [it not to be]." "<b>חגורים</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, מתניכם חגורים, and the other in the matter of the idol of Micah — ושש מאות איש חגורים. And this is what they expounded, that the idol of Micah crossed the sea with them, that even when they were girded to go, the idol was with them. And the other in Daniel — והנה איש אחד לבוש בדים ומתניו חגורים — to say that even though there were wicked among them, the righteous among them are like the ministering angels." "<b>בחפזון</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and כי בחפזון יצאת מארץ מצרים, and כי לא בחפזון תצאו. And this is what they expounded, that it was not in haste of Israel, as it is written כי לא בחפזון תצאו."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:36.278073317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}